WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:06.240
Over the last few days, democratic presidential
candidate Pete Buddha judge was involved in

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.150
some really strange exchanges and most of
them have to do with money in politics, campaign

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.770
finance, uh, transparency and it does not
look good for mayor Pete.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:21.490
The first one is at a press conference before
or after an event and he's asked about why

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.130
won't you open up fundraisers to the press?

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.210
He's very Curt and he says he doesn't have
a timeline for when he's going to consider

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.210
doing that.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.210
He's then asked to follow up.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.050
Well, you're the candidate, can't you just
tell your campaign to open them up to the

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.050
press?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.839
And mayor Pete says, yes, but there are considerations.

00:00:35.839 --> 00:00:38.510
And then he's asked as another followup, what
are the considerations?

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.649
And he says, I'm not going to tell you.

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:41.649
Take a look at this.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:42.649
Yeah.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:47.190
Earlier today you said you were open to having
a conversation about opening or fundraisers.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.109
And that's a question that reporters have
been asking me for months now.

00:00:51.109 --> 00:00:58.629
So I'm wondering when do you expect to be,
to actually have that conversation and give

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:06.300
like stance on that as, as the candidate Kevin
just directed.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.420
Yes.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.350
And what happens with that?

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.899
And I'm thinking about it, last question,
can you give us an example of those considerations?

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:17.689
No, thank you.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:20.409
Thank you.

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:25.590
Is this a strategy of some kind because it
comes off looking absolutely terrible.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:30.270
Doing close to the press events I don't actually
think is problematic in principle.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.840
It's actually a good thing for elected officials
and candidates to be able to talk to voters

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.679
privately without the press there.

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:42.149
I think that that's generally speaking a good
thing, uh, but in some instances, but when

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:47.030
it's big money fundraisers and there's already
slipperiness coming from Pete about campaign

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.960
finance and then this is how he answers the
questions.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.249
It doesn't look good.

00:01:51.249 --> 00:01:52.619
Here's another video.

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:57.359
We're a student activist named Greg Chung
asks, P Buddha judge, when we talk about getting

00:01:57.359 --> 00:02:01.710
money out of politics, shouldn't that include
not taking money from million from billionaires

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.310
and doing closed-door fundraisers?

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.260
And Pete just says, no, that's not what my
getting money out of politics should include.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.319
I know the audio is not great on this one.

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:10.569
The video is subtitled.

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:13.120
Apologies for people who are just listening.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:23.209
I know that it may be hard to understand everything
that's said.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:30.720
[inaudible]

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.040
I saw comments about this saying, Oh, this
is totally tone deaf.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.430
It's not that it's tone deaf, it's that this
is Pete Buddha judge telling us what he really

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.430
believes.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.240
He doesn't want to stop billionaire donations
or private fundraisers because he's a centrist

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.710
status quo guy.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.710
Period.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:52.480
The bar for transparency, particularly on
this issue of money and politics has definitely

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.379
changed in the last few years with more and
more candidates saying they won't accept corporate

00:02:56.379 --> 00:03:00.390
PAC money or uh, money from corporations at
all or whatever.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:03.660
Pete, Buddha, judge and Joe Biden are just
behind on this.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.160
They are completely out of touch with what
is expected now on the progressive left, what

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.930
I do think is good is that in the same way
that Joe Biden isn't pretending to be a super

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.800
progressive, he's running as a centrist and
he is a centrist Pete.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:22.620
Buddha judge is doing the same thing, although
to a lesser degree, yes, Pete is being slippery

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.209
on Medicare for all with this Medicare for
all who want it thing, but on lots of these

00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:29.209
issues.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:34.709
I'm glad that Biden is just telling it to
us like it is and Pete is telling it to us

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:36.829
like it is in their policy.

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:38.189
I disagree with them.

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:44.019
I am well to their left, but one of the things
that's really good is with some candidates

00:03:44.019 --> 00:03:48.450
you get this sense that they're not really
telling us what they actually believe.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.880
This was asserted about Hillary Clinton in
2016 that everything was just what she thought

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.590
would sound best at the time.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:59.041
This has been asserted with other candidates
as well with mayor Pete and Joe Biden, they

00:03:59.041 --> 00:04:00.989
seem to be centrists.

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:03.390
Their policies are Centrus policies.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.819
They are telling us that in public, they're
not hiding behind it.

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:09.799
And I like it because it makes it much easier
for me to figure out.

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:11.160
Both of these guys are well to my right.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.959
They are not the people that I would consider
supporting in a primary.

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:16.200
He's being upfront.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:20.510
It's fine for him to say this, but we need
to do away with the false notion that Buddha

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:24.640
judges any kind of progressive period and
he's making that a very easy notion to do

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.890
away with every time he says something like
this.

